# Copy to `.env.local` for local tooling only. Do not commit real values.
# See also `.env.local.example` (safe to commit) for the Vercel pull workflow.
# Neon + API (from Vercel: vercel env pull .env.local): DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET
# Optional build-time override for the static client (see README):
# WFH_PUBLIC_API_BASE=
# Google sign-in. Create an OAuth web client in Google Cloud and add your Vercel/local origins.
# GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
# WFH_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
# Optional native iOS client ID accepted by the API when the iOS app signs in.
# GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
# Apple sign-in. Use the Services ID for web as the client ID and add the redirect URL in Apple Developer.
# APPLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
# APPLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://your-app.vercel.app/
# Password reset emails (Resend). Without these, forgot-password still returns 200 but does not send mail.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=
# Canonical site URL for reset links if Host / X-Forwarded-* headers are wrong (e.g. some proxies):
# WFH_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://your-app.vercel.app
# Note: NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* vars are not used by this app (legacy); safe to remove from .env.local.
